    {
      "id": "4cQ5hXxCYM6egAlDUHSFg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -215.0820522021413,
      "y": 8897.10580866884,
      "width": 1329.726806640625,
      "height": 1150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f783ac",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b06",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1074925054,
      "version": 6,
      "versionNonce": 610175906,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789464821751,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. What is it?\n\nNon-blocking I/O ka matlab hai:\n\nJab Node.js koi I/O operation start karta hai, toh woh us operation ke complete hone ka wait karke main thread ko block nahi karta.\n\nI/O = Input/Output operations, jaise:\n\nDatabase se data lena\nFile read karna\nNetwork/API request\nExternal service se response lena\n2. Problem kya thi?\n\nMaan lo server ko database se data chahiye aur database response aane mein 3 seconds lagte hain.\n\nBlocking approach mein:\n\nDatabase request start → 3 seconds wait → result mila → next work\n\nIs waiting time mein thread useful work nahi kar pa raha hota.\n\nAgar bahut requests aa jayein, toh waiting ki wajah se resources inefficiently use ho sakte hain.\n\n3. Non-blocking approach kya karti hai?\n\nNode.js mein:\n\nDatabase request start karo → wait mat karo → doosra available work handle karo → database result ready hone par usse handle karo.\n\nYaani main JavaScript thread I/O ke wait mein unnecessarily stuck nahi rehta.\n\n4. Important point\n\nNon-blocking ka matlab ye nahi hai ki I/O operation instantly complete ho jata hai.\n\nOperation ko time lag sakta hai.\n\nDifference sirf itna hai:\n\nMain JavaScript execution uske complete hone tak unnecessarily wait nahi karta.\n\n5. Main benefit\nMultiple I/O operations efficiently handle ho sakte hain.\nServer I/O ke wait mein unnecessarily block nahi hota.\nHigh-concurrency, I/O-heavy applications ke liye useful hai.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. What is it?\n\nNon-blocking I/O ka matlab hai:\n\nJab Node.js koi I/O operation start karta hai, toh woh us operation ke complete hone ka wait karke main thread ko block nahi karta.\n\nI/O = Input/Output operations, jaise:\n\nDatabase se data lena\nFile read karna\nNetwork/API request\nExternal service se response lena\n2. Problem kya thi?\n\nMaan lo server ko database se data chahiye aur database response aane mein 3 seconds lagte hain.\n\nBlocking approach mein:\n\nDatabase request start → 3 seconds wait → result mila → next work\n\nIs waiting time mein thread useful work nahi kar pa raha hota.\n\nAgar bahut requests aa jayein, toh waiting ki wajah se resources inefficiently use ho sakte hain.\n\n3. Non-blocking approach kya karti hai?\n\nNode.js mein:\n\nDatabase request start karo → wait mat karo → doosra available work handle karo → database result ready hone par usse handle karo.\n\nYaani main JavaScript thread I/O ke wait mein unnecessarily stuck nahi rehta.\n\n4. Important point\n\nNon-blocking ka matlab ye nahi hai ki I/O operation instantly complete ho jata hai.\n\nOperation ko time lag sakta hai.\n\nDifference sirf itna hai:\n\nMain JavaScript execution uske complete hone tak unnecessarily wait nahi karta.\n\n5. Main benefit\nMultiple I/O operations efficiently handle ho sakte hain.\nServer I/O ke wait mein unnecessarily block nahi hota.\nHigh-concurrency, I/O-heavy applications ke liye useful hai.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
