    {
      "id": "0kowP7n5jXDoUuB5IqKR6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -98.74992931541419,
      "y": 10175.250367983166,
      "width": 1474.064066744181,
      "height": 561.9630197308607,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#40c057",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b08",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1054956734,
      "version": 121,
      "versionNonce": 810153634,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789464894647,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "| Point              | Synchronous                                        | Asynchronous                                                                  |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Meaning**        | Work **sequence mein** hota hai                    | Work start karke **wait kiye bina** next work ho sakta hai\n|\n| **Execution**      | Next task previous task ke complete hone ke baad   | Next task previous task ke complete hone ka wait nahi karta\n|\n| **Waiting**        | Waiting/blocking ho sakti hai                      | I/O ke case mein unnecessary waiting avoid hoti hai\n|\n| **Flow**           | **Task A → wait → Task B**                         | **Task A start → Task B → A complete hone par result handle**\n|\n| **Example**        | File read karo → result aane tak wait → next code  | File read start karo → doosra code chalao → result ready hone\npar handle karo |\n| **I/O operations** | I/O wait ke dauran execution block ho sakta hai    | I/O ke dauran other work continue ho sakta hai\n|\n| **Node.js**        | Synchronous code Event Loop ko block kar sakta hai | Node.js mein asynchronous I/O commonly use hota hai\n|\n| **Main benefit**   | Simple aur predictable flow                        | Better concurrency aur responsiveness\n|\n| **Main issue**     | Slow operation poore flow ko delay kar sakta hai   | Flow aur error handling comparatively complex ho sakti hai\n|\n",
      "fontSize": 21.40811503736612,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "| Point              | Synchronous                                        | Asynchronous                                                                  |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Meaning**        | Work **sequence mein** hota hai                    | Work start karke **wait kiye bina** next work ho sakta hai                    |\n| **Execution**      | Next task previous task ke complete hone ke baad   | Next task previous task ke complete hone ka wait nahi karta                   |\n| **Waiting**        | Waiting/blocking ho sakti hai                      | I/O ke case mein unnecessary waiting avoid hoti hai                           |\n| **Flow**           | **Task A → wait → Task B**                         | **Task A start → Task B → A complete hone par result handle**                 |\n| **Example**        | File read karo → result aane tak wait → next code  | File read start karo → doosra code chalao → result ready hone par handle karo |\n| **I/O operations** | I/O wait ke dauran execution block ho sakta hai    | I/O ke dauran other work continue ho sakta hai                                |\n| **Node.js**        | Synchronous code Event Loop ko block kar sakta hai | Node.js mein asynchronous I/O commonly use hota hai                           |\n| **Main benefit**   | Simple aur predictable flow                        | Better concurrency aur responsiveness                                         |\n| **Main issue**     | Slow operation poore flow ko delay kar sakta hai   | Flow aur error handling comparatively complex ho sakti hai                    |\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
